[tool_result] toolu_01XdgGQvvvC8d4ttjRpJD2xa [{"type":"text","text":"Plan follows.\n\n---\n\n# Phase 2b.2 implementation plan — QR-code pairing flow\n\n## 1. Library choice\n\nConfirm the memo's pick: **`jsqr` for decode, `qrcode` for encode**. Both are pure-JS, no native bindings, MIT/Apache, actively maintained, and tree-shakeable.\n\n- `jsqr` ~43 KB min / ~13 KB gzip — single function `jsQR(imageData, w, h, opts)`.\n- `qrcode` ~50 KB min / ~17 KB gzip — `QRCode.toCanvas(el, text)` / `QRCode.toDataURL(text)`.\n\nCombined raw weight ~30 KB gzip lives entirely inside the lazy-loaded PairScreen chunk; main bundle untouched. Alternatives considered and rejected: `@zxing/library` (huge, ~250 KB), `qr-scanner` (wraps jsqr, no win), DIY (out of scope).\n\n## 2. Compression strategy\n\nUse **native `CompressionStream('gzip')` + `DecompressionStream('gzip')` + base64url**. No `pako`.\n\n- Browser support: Chrome 80+, Safari 16.4+, Firefox 113+, all current Android Chrome and Edge. Both ends of this app are modern browsers on devices the
